            "description": "Watch Universitario vs Club Nacional highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on April 29, 2026. High stakes and an intense continental atmosphere defined the encounter between Universitario and Club Nacional in the CONMEBOL Libertadores . Both sides entered the pitch knowing that every tactical decision and individual error would be magnified under the floodlights of this prestigious tournament. Early Drama and the Red Card Turning Point The match, held on May 30, 2026 , ignited early in the first half when Club Nacional was awarded a penalty in the 14th minute. Maximiliano Gomez stepped up to the spot and clinically converted the chance, giving the visitors an early lead and silencing the home supporters. However, the physical nature of the contest soon became a major factor, with Cain Jair Fara and Lucas Rodriguez picking up early bookings. The defining moment of the first half arrived in the 35th minute when Rodriguez was shown his second yellow card, leaving Nacional to defend their lead with only ten men for the remainder of the evening. Universitario wasted little time in exploiting their numerical superiority. In the 40th minute, Jairo Concha provided a pinpoint assist for Cain Jair Fara , who made amends for his earlier booking by leveling the score. The momentum had shifted entirely, and the hosts headed into the break with the wind in their sails after a frantic opening 45 minutes. Second Half Surges and Tactical Shifts The second half began with a lightning strike from the home side. Only a minute after the restart, Alex Valera found the back of the net to put Universitario 2-1 ahead, completing a swift turnaround. Despite the setback and the man disadvantage, Club Nacional refused to collapse. Tactical substitutions saw the introduction of Maximiliano Silvera , and the move paid immediate dividends. In the 71st minute, Silvera stunned the stadium with an equalizer, dragging the ten-man Uruguayan side back into the game at 2-2. As the clock ticked down, the tension escalated, leading to further yellow cards for Luis Mejia and Jorge Murrugarra . Universitario manager responded by introducing Lisandro Alzugaray , a change that would prove decisive. In the 81st minute, Alzugaray struck a crucial goal to restore the lead for the hosts, sparking wild celebrations that earned him a yellow card just moments later. Stoppage Time Drama Seals the Win With Club Nacional pushing men forward in a desperate attempt to rescue a point, gaps inevitably opened in their defensive line. Universitario took full advantage of the tired visitors during the seven minutes of added time. In the 91st minute, Hector Fertoli turned provider, setting up Jose Carabali for a composed finish that made it 4-2. This final goal effectively ended the contest, ensuring that Universitario walked away with all three points. It was a match defined by resilience and clinical finishing, where the early dismissal of Lucas Rodriguez proved too heavy a burden for Nacional to overcome despite their spirited second-half comeback attempt."
        },
