            "description": "Watch Universitario vs Deportes Tolima highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 26, 2026. Universitario and Deportes Tolima faced off in a high-voltage CONMEBOL Libertadores clash where tactical discipline and physical endurance were put to the ultimate test. Supporters witnessed a strategic battle defined by intense duels as both managers searched for a decisive breakthrough. Early Adjustments and Tight Marking The match, held on May 26, 2026, began with a frenetic pace as both sides struggled to assert dominance in the midfield. Universitario was forced into an early tactical shift when Hector Fertoli made way for Jorge Murrugarra in the 29th minute, a move aimed at stabilizing the spine of the team against a persistent Deportes Tolima press. Despite several forays into the final third, both defensive lines remained resolute, leading to a goalless first half that concluded after four minutes of stoppage time. Tactical Chess in the Second Half As the second half got underway, the stalemate continued, prompting a series of influential changes from the bench. Deportes Tolima introduced Juan Pablo Torres just after the hour mark, while Universitario responded by bringing on the creative Edison Flores for Lisandro Alzugaray . The game evolved into a tactical chess match, with neither side willing to overcommit and risk a devastating counter-attack, keeping the tension high throughout the stadium. Late Drama and Disciplined Finishes The final fifteen minutes saw a flurry of activity as both managers exhausted their substitution options. A triple change for the visitors in the 77th minute saw Jan Angulo , Kelvin Florez , and Cesar Inga enter the fray, while the hosts introduced Sekou Gassama . The increased physicality of the closing stages resulted in yellow cards for Cristian Arrieta and Juan Pablo Torres . After eight minutes of added time, the referee blew the final whistle on a hard-fought contest that saw the points shared between two determined competitors."
